---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "~/lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contribute to the email spec"
  description="How to propose new topics, corrections, and status changes to The Email Specification, and what every change needs before it is merged."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Contribute</nav>
      <h1>Contribute</h1><p class="lede">
        The spec is <a href={site.repo} rel="external">open on GitHub</a>. Issues, pull
        requests, and disagreements are welcome. Three rules.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <article class="narrow section prose">
    <h2 id="cite-your-sources">1. Cite your sources</h2>
    <p>
      Every topic lists at least one source. If you add or change a claim, link the RFC, the
      W3C guidance, or the provider documentation behind it. No source, no merge.
    </p>

    <h2 id="stay-provider-agnostic">2. Stay provider-agnostic</h2>
    <p>
      The spec describes outcomes, not one provider's implementation. “Publish a DMARC
      policy” is in scope. “Click this toggle in your ESP's dashboard” is not; link to the
      provider's own documentation instead.
    </p>

    <h2 id="be-honest-about-status">3. Be honest about status</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Required</strong> means mail breaks or excludes people without it. <strong
        >Recommended</strong
      > means a modern sender should do it. <strong>Optional</strong> means it depends.
      <strong>Avoid</strong> means it is outdated or harmful. If a status is wrong, fix it, with
      your reasoning in the pull request.
    </p>

    <h2 id="how-to-propose-a-change">How to propose a change</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open an <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`} rel="external">issue</a> describing the topic,
        gap, or fix.
      </li>
      <li>
        For a new topic, copy an existing file in <code
          >src/content/spec/&lt;category&gt;/</code
        > and adjust the front matter.
      </li>
      <li>
        Add a dated entry under <code>src/content/changelog/</code> for any material change.
      </li>
      <li>
        Run <code>npm run dev</code> locally on port 31337 and check the page renders. Before
        you open the pull request, run <code>npm run build</code>, <code>npm run check</code
        >,
        <code>npm run mcp:typecheck</code>, and <code>npm run mcp:dry-run</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open a pull request. CI checks formatting and types, and builds the site and the MCP
        server.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="repository">Repository</h2>
    <p><a href={site.repo} rel="external">{site.repo}</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
